services/acquisition/*.jsonl
# The published directory IS committed, deliberately.
#
# /places used to be the only reader and it degraded to an empty state, so this
# file was treated as a build artifact. It is not one any more: the homepage's
# listing grid and every /stay page read it, so without it in the repository a
# fresh clone - and a Vercel deploy, which has no crawl step - renders an empty
# site. Committing it means the deploy shows real observed inventory, and
# re-running the crawl updates it as a reviewable diff.
#
# Regenerate with:
#   python pipeline.py --states LA,FC,OY,IM,AK --publish directory.json
# or, without re-fetching anything, from a frozen stage:
#   python pipeline.py --publish-from records-npc.jsonl --publish directory.json
services/acquisition/ingest-report.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Staged rollout artifacts: crawl output, resume marks and per-stage ingest reports.
records-*.jsonl
done-*.txt
rollout-*.json
ingest-*.json
*.log
